{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:LiftingAndDescent.OrderingJetCompatibility","@type":"LeanModule","name":"LiftingAndDescent.OrderingJetCompatibility","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Order.WellFounded","lean:module:Mathlib.Order.WellFoundedSet","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.List.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.List.Lex"],"declarations":13,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.ordering_jet_compatibility","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.ordering_jet_compatibility","kind":"def","line":194,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/ordering-jet-compatibility.lean#L194-L201","doc":"**Consequence for time**: the braiding-induced ordering ≺_c on\nA₀ propagates through the entire jet tower. Forward time\n(Gröbner reduction, braiding) and backward time (anti-involution,\nunbraiding) are well-defined at every brane level. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.direct_limit_terminates","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.direct_limit_terminates","kind":"axiom","line":184,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/ordering-jet-compatibility.lean#L184-L192","doc":"The direct limit algebra A_∞ = colim End(A_n) carries a filtered\nadmissible ordering ≺_∞ = ⋃_n ≺_n. The Gröbner reduction\nalgorithm terminates on every element belonging to some finite\nlevel A_n. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.wellfounded_at_level","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.wellfounded_at_level","kind":"theorem","line":176,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/ordering-jet-compatibility.lean#L176-L182","doc":"Well-foundedness at each level n: no infinite descending chains\nin B_n.  Immediate from `degLex_wellFounded`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.ordering_compatible","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.ordering_compatible","kind":"axiom","line":168,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/ordering-jet-compatibility.lean#L168-L174","doc":"Left and right compatibility with multiplication at each level:\na ≺ b implies c·a·d ≺ c·b·d (when products are nonzero). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.ordering_extends","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.ordering_extends","kind":"theorem","line":144,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/ordering-jet-compatibility.lean#L144-L166","doc":"**The former `ordering_extends` axiom was `P → P`.**\n\nIt stood as an `axiom` for\n\n    (k : ℕ) (a b : MonomialBasis) (hab : degLex a b) : degLex a b\n\n-- the conclusion is the hypothesis, so `exact hab` closes it and the\naxiom asserted nothing.  `k` did not appear in the statement at all.\n\nThe docstring described a different claim: *\"if `a ≺_n b` in `B_n`,\nthen `ℓ_n(a) ≺_{n+1} ℓ_n(b)` in `B_{n+1}`\"*.  The jet embedding\n`ℓ_n` occurs nowhere in the type, and neither does the level index,\nso nothing about prolongation was ever stated.\n\nStating it needs `ℓ_n` as a map `MonomialBasis → MonomialBasis` and\na hypothesis relating `degLex` across it; that is a real claim and\nis left open rather than replaced by a guess.  The identity below is\nkept only so the name resolves and the vacuity is on the record. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.JetExtension.numNewDirs","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.JetExtension.numNewDirs","kind":"def","line":142,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/ordering-jet-compatibility.lean#L142-L142","doc":"Number of new Ω¹ directions per prolongation (= 3 for SU(2)). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.JetExtension.numGens","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.JetExtension.numGens","kind":"def","line":140,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/ordering-jet-compatibility.lean#L140-L140","doc":"Number of generators at this level. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.JetExtension.level","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.JetExtension.level","kind":"def","line":138,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/ordering-jet-compatibility.lean#L138-L138","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.JetExtension.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.JetExtension.mk","kind":"ctor","line":137,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/ordering-jet-compatibility.lean#L137-L137","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.JetExtension","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.JetExtension","kind":"structure","line":133,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/ordering-jet-compatibility.lean#L133-L142","doc":"At brane level k, the jet prolongation introduces new generators\n(Ω¹ directions) ordered after all level-k generators. The\nresulting ordering on B_{k+1} extends B_k. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.degLex_wellFounded","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.degLex_wellFounded","kind":"theorem","line":125,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/ordering-jet-compatibility.lean#L125-L131","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:ordering-jet-compatibility","label":"prop:ordering-jet-compatibility","md":"quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/ordering-jet-compatibility.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.degLex","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.degLex","kind":"def","line":29,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/ordering-jet-compatibility.lean#L29-L35","doc":"Degree-lexicographic ordering on braid monomials:\ncompare by length first, then lexicographically. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.MonomialBasis","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.MonomialBasis","kind":"def","line":24,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/ordering-jet-compatibility.lean#L24-L27","doc":"A monomial basis element: a reduced positive braid word\n(list of generator indices). ","signatureChunk":0}]}